 "note": "Former Office of the Department of Agriculture (1931 Agricultural Bank; ArtGeo Gallery), 7 Queen St on the Marine Tce corner, State Register 00405. Part of the Saltwater project: the City is turning it into the centre's bar and restaurant. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), a 2021 Mapillary view from the roundabout and the inHerit record: red stretcher-bond brick under a hipped terracotta tile roof with boxed eaves, the narrow end to Queen St with a symmetrical front of two big twelve-pane windows and a cream rendered porch (arched sides), a rendered frieze lettered AGRICULTURE WESTERN AUSTRALIA, six sash windows down each side, a rendered chimney on the south side. The small dark-roofed back-of-house block behind it (Saltwater's admin) rides along as an outbuilding. Plain lettering only. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen St (north to south), y back (east) from the porch front.",
